_The slug is REQUIRED and lives on the Promote tab, so a page cannot be saved from the Content tab alone._

**Slug (\`slug\`):**

sf.gov/departments--healthy-housing-and-vector-control--about

**Title tag (\`seo_title\`):**

About Healthy Housing and Vector Control | SF.gov

**Meta description (\`search_description\`):**

Learn who the Healthy Housing and Vector Control team is, what they do, and how the program is organized.

## Unmapped — no documented Karl destination

Nothing below has a field to be typed into. It is listed rather than dropped, because an absence reads as "there was nothing there".

- \`summary\` — The page carries \`summary\`, and no About us panel documented in the field map accepts it.
- \`audience\` — The page carries \`audience\`, and the panel SF.gov puts it in is not on this type. About us has no \`things_to_know\` panel — it is Transaction-only — and no free-text intro either, so the audience has to move into the body copy or be dropped deliberately. Confirmed on a published page — sf.gov/manage-covid-19-schools-childcare-and-youth-programs renders "Who this information is for" as an H3 inside its grey "What to know" box, with the audiences as a bulleted list.
