"# Article 11 compliance for property owners — Karl transcript

**Karl path:** New: Information → Content
**Decision:** no review recorded
**Page key:** \`article11Compliance\` · **Slug:** \`sf.gov/information--article-11-compliance-for-property-owners\` · **Type:** Information

**NOT APPROVED — do not publish from this transcript.** Approval in this tool is per page, not per field, so nothing below is signed off.

> Every keystroke below is yours to make. This file is an export, not an approval, and nothing here has been written to Karl.

### Page title — \`title\` [TYPE] — page not approved

**Page title:**

Article 11 compliance for property owners

### Description — \`description\` [TYPE] — page not approved

**Description:**

See what landlords and managers must do under the Health Code, plus the yearly fee and who to call.

### Primary agency — \`primary_agency\` [FLAG] — page not approved

_U6 — supply the parent Agency page by hand; the mockup has no field for it._

### Information section — \`information_section\` [TYPE] — page not approved

_The Title "Who this information is for" is not in the mockup — this tool supplies it, matching sf.gov/manage-covid-19-schools-childcare-and-youth-programs, which renders the audience as an H3 with that title over a bulleted list. Add this block first, so every authored section below is one Information section block later than its place among the mockup sections._

**Title:**

Who this information is for

**Text:**

- This page is for property owners and managers responsible for Article 11 compliance.

### Information section — \`information_section\` [TYPE] — page not approved

**Title:**

What Article 11 requires

**Text:**

San Francisco Health Code Article 11 requires property owners and managers to keep buildings free of public health nuisances. These include pests, garbage, mold, and rodent problems.

- Pay your annual Healthy Housing fee if your building has 3 or more rental units
- Investigate tenant pest reports within 72 hours, and write every report down in a log
- Hire a licensed pest control operator (PCO) for treatment — never unlicensed staff
- Keep records of complaints, inspections, and treatments for at least 2 years
- Notify tenants in writing before pesticide application
- Complete pest-management training if you have repeat violations

### Information section — \`information_section\` [TYPE] — page not approved

**Title:**

If you get a report or notice

**Text:**

When a tenant reports a pest or housing health problem, owners and managers must start investigating within 72 hours.

If Environmental Health finds a violation, they issue a notice of violation (NOV). It lists the required corrections and a compliance deadline.

- [Correct a violation and close your case](stepCorrectViolation)
- [What happens after you report](afterReport)

**Links in this text — recreate each with the Link tool, do not paste them:**

- "Correct a violation and close your case" → shape 5 — rich text Link tool → Internal link → "Correct a violation and close your case"
- "What happens after you report" → shape 5 — rich text Link tool → Internal link → "What happens after you report a housing or pest problem"

### Information section — \`information_section\` [TYPE] — page not approved

**Title:**

What you must do

**Text:**

These requirements come from Article 11 and the San Francisco Department of Public Health (SFDPH) Director's Rules and Regulations.

- Investigate tenant pest reports within 72 hours of receiving them.
- Keep a written log of every report or sign of vermin: rodents, fleas, flies, bedbugs, spiders, cockroaches, wasps, and mosquitoes. Give the log to your pest control operator. You can use the City's [complaint forms and log template](https://www.sf.gov/resource/2024/healthy-housing-and-pest-information).
- Keep records of complaints, inspections, and pest control services for at least 2 years. Make them available to the Department of Public Health on request.
- Hire only licensed pest control operators (PCOs) to apply pesticides or trap rats. Never use unlicensed staff or over-the-counter treatments for significant infestations.
- Give tenants written notice before pesticide application, including the product name, date, and safety information.
- Complete pest-management training if the Director requires it after repeat violations.
- [See the full owner-responsibility table](article11Guide)

**Links in this text — recreate each with the Link tool, do not paste them:**

- "complaint forms and log template" → shape 5 — rich text Link tool → External link
- "See the full owner-responsibility table" → shape 5 — rich text Link tool → Internal link → "Health Code Article 11 in plain language"

### Information section — \`information_section\` [TYPE] — page not approved

**Title:**

Fees and full requirements

**Text:**

Buildings with 3 or more rental units pay an annual Healthy Housing fee. Current certified rates range from $103 to $808 or more, depending on unit count.

- [See the full fee schedule for exact tier amounts and reinspection rates](payFee)
- [See the full Article 11 guide for the complete section-by-section mapping](article11Guide)

**Links in this text — recreate each with the Link tool, do not paste them:**

- "See the full fee schedule for exact tier amounts and reinspection rates" → shape 5 — rich text Link tool → Internal link → "Pay your annual Healthy Housing fee for apartment buildings"
- "See the full Article 11 guide for the complete section-by-section mapping" → shape 5 — rich text Link tool → Internal link → "Health Code Article 11 in plain language"

### Information section — \`information_section\` [TYPE] — page not approved

**Title:**

Legal authority

**Text:**

Article 11 defines these requirements and how HHVC enforces them.

- **Sec. 581:** Defines the public health nuisances covered by this article, including pest, garbage, mold, and rodent conditions.
- **Sec. 596:** Sets the complaint, inspection, and Notice of Violation (NOV) process.
- **Sec. 600:** Authorizes criminal, civil, and administrative penalties of up to $1,000 per violation per day.
- [View Health Code Article 11 on municode](https://codelibrary.amlegal.com/codes/san_francisco/latest/sf_health/0-0-0-1890)
- [See the full section-by-section mapping](article11Guide)

**Links in this text — recreate each with the Link tool, do not paste them:**

- "View Health Code Article 11 on municode" → shape 5 — rich text Link tool → External link
- "See the full section-by-section mapping" → shape 5 — rich text Link tool → Internal link → "Health Code Article 11 in plain language"

