Free

### Things to Know — \`things_to_know\` [TYPE] — page not approved

**Block 1 — Title:**

Reporting anonymously

**Block 1 — Text:**

You can report anonymously. 311 does not require your name. We never share your name or contact information.

**Block 2 — Title:**

Seeing a dead bird

**Block 2 — Text:**

Report it to the State West Nile virus program instead of 311 — dead birds help track West Nile virus.

### What to Do — \`what_to_do\` [TYPE] — page not approved

_The mockup heading "What to do" is not typed anywhere — Karl's What to Do panel carries its own label. Each step below becomes one Section block._

_A step with text, a button and a callout becomes ONE Section block whose Section specifics holds a Text, a Button link and a Callout as siblings — not fields on the step._

**Section 1 — Section title:**

Start your report

**Section 1 — Section specifics → Text:**

Use 311 to report an active problem to the City.

If the problem is urgent, report now.

**Section 1 — Section specifics → Button link → Link text:**

Report through 311

**Section 1 — Button link → destination:**

None

**Section 2 — Section title:**

Notify your landlord before reporting

**Section 2 — Section specifics → Text:**

- **Notify your landlord:** Tell the property owner or manager about the insects. For bed bugs, owners must investigate complaints promptly and coordinate treatment.
- **Give them 72 hours:** If they do not start fixing the problem within 3 days, report it to the City.
- **Urgent problems:** If there is a serious danger to health or safety, report it right away without waiting.

**Section 3 — Section title:**

Tell us where the problem is

**Section 3 — Section specifics → Text:**

Only share the details that apply to your situation:

- **What you saw:** Cockroaches, bed bugs, mosquitoes, flies, wasps, mites, or another insect problem.
- **Where it is:** The address or location, and where you saw the insects (inside, outside, or in a shared area).
- **Standing water:** For mosquitoes, tell us about any standing water — buckets, planters, clogged gutters, or fountains.
- **When it started:** How long this has been happening.
- **Landlord notice:** If you rent, tell us if you already notified the property owner or manager.
- **Your contact info:** Leave your name and phone number or email if you want an inspector to contact you.

**Section 3 — Section specifics → Button link → Link text:**

Report a dead bird

**Section 3 — Button link → destination:**

External URL → https://westnile.ca.gov/report

**Callout (rich text, no title field):**

See a dead bird? Report it to the State West Nile virus program instead — dead birds help track West Nile virus.

### Accordion title and text — \`supporting_information\` [TYPE] — page not approved

**Title:**

While you wait: tips to help with the problem

**Text:**

It may take us a few weekdays to get back to you. In the meantime, here are a few things you can do to help with the problem.

- **Cockroaches:** Clean up crumbs and grease, fix dripping faucets and leaks, and seal cracks near pipes. Use bait stations instead of sprays.
- **Bed bugs:** Do not throw out furniture before treatment — it can spread the bugs. Wash and dry bedding on high heat, and tell your landlord right away.
- **Mosquitoes:** Dump standing water at least once a week — buckets, planters, saucers, and clogged gutters. Fix holes in window screens.
- **Flies:** Bag garbage tightly and keep bin lids closed so flies cannot breed in it.
- **Wasps:** Do not disturb a ground nest. Mark the spot and keep people and pets away until it is treated.

### Custom Section — \`custom_section\` [TYPE] — page not approved

⚠ Inferred mapping — verify the destination before saving.

_Inferred mapping — the field map documents this panel only for supporting/flat sections. Transaction has no generic body stream and this is its only repeatable Title-and-text panel, so verify the destination before saving._

**Title:**

Get help making your report

**Text:**

You can make a report even if you are not the tenant. A friend, family member, advocate, or helper can report for someone else.

- You can ask 311 for help in your language.
- You can ask 311 for a service request number so you can follow up later.

### Custom Section — \`custom_section\` [TYPE] — page not approved

