- "Report a problem in an SRO or hotel" → shape 5 — rich text Link tool → Internal link → "Report a problem in an SRO or hotel"
- "Report a dead bird to the State West Nile virus program" → shape 5 — rich text Link tool → External link
- "Read Article 11 in plain language" → shape 5 — rich text Link tool → Internal link → "Health Code Article 11 in plain language"

### Information section — \`information_section\` [TYPE] — page not approved

**Title:**

If your problem is not listed

**Text:**

- Some housing problems are handled by other City programs. For example, structural water intrusion, leaks, and major heating or utility failures go to the [Department of Building Inspection (DBI)](#). DBI handles these under the San Francisco Housing Code (2025).
- If your problem is not on this list, start with 311. They can send your report to the right place.
- For lead, pesticides, water quality, food sanitation, or business hygiene, use the [Citywide health nuisance and hazards reporting service](https://www.sf.gov/report-health-nuisance-or-hazards).
- If you are not sure whether HHVC can review your problem, it is still okay to report it. HHVC will review whether it may involve a housing or pest-related public health concern.

